%% Decision 11.8 + decision 012 — checkout. Everything between BEGIN and COMMIT is one Postgres transaction under RLS
%% (buyer context). Side effects are pg-boss jobs enqueued INSIDE the same transaction.
%% Updated D4-B4 (26.11): purchase mode per supplier group (no paymentMethod), stock check before the transaction,
%% contract check for direct, ledger and pro-forma per mode, card payment and supplier submission after commit.
%% The gateway and supplier-API steps (mock-services) are built in D9-D10; the database steps follow migrations 0004-0005.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor B as Buyer (owner or member)
  participant UI as Checkout page
  participant SA as Server Action (next-safe-action)
  participant SUP as Supplier stock API (mock-services)
  participant D as createOrder(source = cart)
  participant PG as PostgreSQL (horeca_app, RLS)
  participant Q as pg-boss queue (in PostgreSQL)
  participant W as Worker (horeca_worker)
  participant GW as Card gateway (mock-services)

  B->>UI: Place order (N supplier groups, each: order directly under contract, or pay by card)
  UI->>SA: idempotencyKey, deliveryLocationId, mode per supplier group, notes
  SA->>SA: Zod validate, resolveActor() from session + member re-check
  SA->>SUP: fresh stock check per supplier (2-3 s timeout, before the transaction)
  SUP-->>SA: ok, or unknown when the API is down (that group cannot be ordered, the others can)
  SA->>PG: BEGIN, then set_config(app.user_id, app.org_id, app.org_type, app.role)
  SA->>D: createOrder(tx, actor, input)
  D->>PG: SELECT order WHERE (buyer_org_id, idempotency_key)
  alt key already used
    D-->>SA: same request_hash: existing order / different hash: Validation error
  else new checkout
    D->>PG: SELECT cart_items ... FOR UPDATE (the only lock: FOR SHARE on products returns 0 rows for a buyer)
    D->>PG: SELECT products, supplier org_profiles, supplier_agreements
    D->>D: revalidate every line: active, supplier approved, min qty + step, PricingResolver price = price seen, buyer tax ID differs from supplier tax ID; mode direct: agreement with that supplier is active
    alt anything changed
      D-->>SA: Conflict with changedLines (nothing written)
    else all valid
      D->>D: splitBySupplier(), money.ts: line VAT, totals, commission (app.resolve_commission_bps)
      D->>PG: INSERT orders (in_progress, unpaid), sub_orders (mode, supplier_submission pending, unpaid), order_lines, sub_order_events
      D->>PG: INSERT ledger_entries per sub-order: platform = sale +gross and commission -commission, direct = commission -commission only
      D->>PG: app.recompute_order() (an order with no platform sub-order becomes not_applicable)
      opt at least one platform sub-order
        D->>PG: app.next_invoice_number() (sequence) then INSERT proforma_invoices for the platform part only (no PDF yet)
      end
      D->>PG: DELETE cart_items
      D->>Q: enqueue(tx): mail buyer, mail suppliers and submit direct sub-orders to the supplier API, render pro-forma PDF (IDs only)
    end
  end
  SA->>PG: COMMIT (rollback on any error: nothing persisted, no job queued)
  opt platform part exists
    SA->>GW: createPayment for the platform part (after commit, 2-3 s timeout; on failure the order page offers Pay now)
    GW-->>SA: hosted card page URL
  end
  SA-->>UI: ok + orderId (+ card page URL), or error code + message + changedLines
  Q->>W: email jobs, supplier submission of direct sub-orders, invoice.render(invoiceId)
  W->>PG: withSystemTx: read invoice snapshot
  W->>W: Playwright HTML to PDF (once)
  W->>PG: UPDATE proforma_invoices SET storage_key (idempotent: skip if already set)
  B->>GW: pays on the hosted card page (test cards only)
  GW->>SA: signed callback (HMAC checked on the raw body), the handler only enqueues one job and answers 200
  Q->>W: payment event job
  W->>PG: withSystemTx: payment_events, order_payments receipt, app.recompute_order() (order becomes paid)
  W->>SUP: submit the platform sub-orders (rejected line: app.system_cancel_sub_order, refund if paid)
